2d/xsp_wiener.en:
``a`` sweeps the neighbourhood window size over the odd values 3, 5, 7, 9 (``k = 3 + 2*int(a*3)``;
a=0 gives 3, a close to 1 gives 9). ``b`` is unused. An adaptive filter that automatically estimates the noise variance
from the local variance; unlike the Gaussian/mean box, which even out with uniform strength,
it evens out flat regions more strongly, while regions of large variance (with many edges/textures)
tend to be preserved. Since it assumes Gaussian noise, it is unsuitable for salt-and-pepper noise.
The output is clipped to [0,1].

2d/xkor_gaussian.en:
a sweeps sigma over the range 0.3–3.0 (``0.3 + 2.7 * a``). b is unused.
On the CPU it is not faster than the scipy version (an implementation that pays off on GPU / batch execution;
with ``IMGEVOLVE_KORNIA_DEVICE=cuda`` it runs on the GPU).

2d/xkor_gaussian.de:
a variiert sigma im Bereich 0.3–3.0 (``0.3 + 2.7 * a``). b wird nicht verwendet.
Auf der CPU ist es nicht schneller als die scipy-Version (eine Implementierung, die sich bei GPU- bzw. Batch-Ausführung lohnt;
mit ``IMGEVOLVE_KORNIA_DEVICE=cuda`` läuft es auf der GPU).

2d/xkor_gaussian.hi:
a, sigma को 0.3–3.0 की range में sweep करता है (``0.3 + 2.7 * a``)। b उपयोग नहीं होता।
CPU पर यह scipy संस्करण से तेज़ नहीं है (यह implementation GPU / batch execution में फ़ायदा देता है;
``IMGEVOLVE_KORNIA_DEVICE=cuda`` के साथ यह GPU पर चलता है)।

2d/xsk_unwrap_phase.en:
``a``, ``b`` are unused. An op used to make phase images that wrap periodically, such as interference fringes, continuous;
for inputs that are not phase-like to begin with, such as a uniform gradient or random noise, it may not give a meaningful
result.

2d/xsk_unwrap_phase.de:
``a``, ``b`` werden nicht verwendet. Ein op, um periodisch umgebrochene Phasenbilder wie Interferenzstreifen stetig zu machen;
bei Eingaben, die von vornherein nicht phasenartig sind, etwa ein gleichmäßiger Verlauf oder zufälliges Rauschen, entsteht möglicherweise kein sinnvolles
Ergebnis.

3d/angle_between_lines.en:
Returns ``arccos(|d̂1·d̂2|)`` in degrees (float). Because the absolute value is taken it lies in **[0, 90]** (forward/backward direction is not distinguished;
if you need the obtuse side, take ``180 −``). ``d1``, ``d2`` are direction vectors (length does not matter, normalised internally),
numeric 2- or 3-vectors; mixed dimensions raise ValueError. A zero vector returns 90.
Uses: parallelism and perpendicularity checks between directions of ``fit_line_3d`` / ``line_from_2points`` (the closer to 0, the more
parallel; the closer to 90, the more orthogonal).

shape2d/invariants.en:
The (major axis, minor axis) of each harmonic's ellipse = its singular values, listed. It contains no DC, so it is invariant to translation;
being singular values, it is invariant to spatial rotation and start-point shift; dividing by the major axis of the 1st harmonic makes it scale
invariant. The foundation of shape matching (:func:`descriptor_distance`).

live4d/focus_sweep_height_video.en:
Focus measure is the mean of the absolute local Laplacian (``window``, Sum-Modified-Laplacian); the height of each pixel is the z of maximum focus
refined to sub-voxel precision with a parabola (a time-series version of ``depth_from_focus``). Use this when you want numbers;
when you want a picture, ``focus_sweep_surface_video``. Pixels without texture have a flat focus measure and their height is undetermined.
